[HIGH] OBF-020 Dynamic command name
    The command word is an expansion the scanner cannot resolve (${x:1:3}, ${x//a/b}, ${x#p}, ${a[1]}, $(echo ... | tr ...), "$1") on a line that fetches a URL into a shell, or in front of a package-manager verb (install, add, i). Hiding the command name this way is how a payload dodges name-based rules; ordinary build lines such as ${CC:-gcc} or "${CMAKE[@]}" are not matched.
